Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["INSPECTING A TABULAR OBJECT", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000807301215657*^9, 
  4.000807306058448*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5498e01b-e6c1-4d25-ae4b-\
bcbd6b749c8e"],

Cell["\<\
When a Tabular object is generated (especially when the data is imported from \
a spreadsheet or similar data formats), it is good practice to inspect the \
object for any data errors\
\>", "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000826300999107*^9, 
  4.000826342768283*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ab2ee18c-ddc2-4b79-a945-\
615a28f4351a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["INSPECT THE NUMBER OF OBSEREVATIONS AND VARIABLES", "Subsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000807564083412*^9, 
  4.000807578210075*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"831f8c90-c218-40e9-9468-\
04e1cf4ffee3"],

Cell["\<\
Assuming that the data is in long-from tidy data format, we can determine the \
number of observations (rows) and the number of variables (columns)\
\>", "Item",
